1:# Mid-century modern house (Eichler / Palm Springs): FORM PLAN (architect)
3:Identity: a long, low post-and-beam house in white stucco and dark timber, with a pale near-flat gable roof, deep eaves and beam ends that stick out past them. The street face is blank apart from a tan ledgestone feature wall, a clerestory strip and an orange front door. A flat carport stands to the west with a teal and white car in front of it. The back is all glass, with a kidney pool behind it.
6:Structural rhythm: **beam lines every 3 cells at x = 10,13,16,19,22,25,28,31.** Every post, beam and beam end sits on one of these lines.
8:## SITE
25:| CARPORT | 0..9 | 1..5 | 7..21 | flat roof deck y=5 on posts; open N, W; screen at S |
26:| Carport posts | x=1 | 1..4 | z=8, 14, 20 | dark_oak_log, 1x1 |
37:| Mailbox | 9 | 1..2 | 1 | low post + box at the head of the driveway |
39:## ROOFS
58:## FACADES
65:| Body | 2..4 | white stucco, glass or posts |
71:- **x=10..17:** blank stucco. In front of it, the **ledgestone feature wall** stands at z=7, x=11..17, y=1..4. It is 1 proud and freestanding, mud_bricks mixed with ~25% packed_mud for the stacked-stone texture. Its top is capped with mud_brick_slab at y=5, but only between the beam lines (x=11,12,14,15,17); the beams at x=13 and x=16 pass over it.
73:- **x=21..31:** stucco with the **clerestory strip** in the top course of the body (y=4): glass at x=22..24, 26..27 and 29..30, and dark_oak_log mullions on the beam lines x=25 and x=28. Below it the wall is blank (bedroom wing).
76:**South (garden, z=25): a wall of glass.** The only stucco is the base (y=1) and the header (y=5). Thin dark posts (dark_oak_log, vertical) stand at y=2..4 on every beam line. Between the posts are full-height glass_pane walls (y=2..4), with sliding-door gaps (see OPENINGS). The eave overhangs to z=27 and the beam ends to z=28.
78:**West (x=10, facing the carport) and East (x=31):** stucco with base and header. Above the header, the gable end shows a glass clerestory band at y=6, z=14..19, between header and roof, and the fascia steps over it. Dark posts at the corners (x=10/31, z=8 and z=25) run y=2..4 on all four corners.
80:**Atrium ring (inner faces):** glass_pane at y=2..4 (and y=6 where the ring crosses band C), with dark_oak_log posts at the 4 ring corners and on x=19 (z=11, z=18). Header y=5: dark_oak_planks.
90:| Glass and posts | flush in the wall plane; the posts read as the wall's structure |
92:## MATERIALS (all ids checked with `mcd blocks --check`)
97:| Structure: posts, beams, beam ends, mullions | dark_oak_log | dark brown, the thin dark posts and exposed beams |
102:| Glass (walls, clerestory, ring) | glass_pane | thin and clear, floor-to-ceiling |
103:| Feature wall | mud_bricks (+25% packed_mud); cap mud_brick_slab | tan desert ledgestone |
123:## OPENINGS (the shell leaves these as air; doors and panes are added by later parts)
129:| North, clerestory | z=8, y=4, x=22..24, 26..27, 29..30 | glass strip, 1h |
132:| West and East, gable clerestory | x=10 and x=31, y=6, z=14..19 | glass, 6w x 1h |
134:| East, bath clerestory | x=31, z=15..16, y=4 | 2w x 1h |
136:| South, living slider | x=14..15, z=25, y=2..3 | 2w x 2h opening, glass at y=4 above |
137:| South, dining/fireplace slider | x=20..21, z=25, y=2..3 | 2w x 2h, glass at y=4 |
138:| South, master slider | x=26..27, z=25, y=2..3 | 2w x 2h, glass at y=4 |
143:## RESERVED (the shell leaves these empty; later parts sink into them or stand on them)
160:## FLOORS
176:| Master bedroom | 23..30 | 21..24 | 2..5 | garden glass and slider |
184:# DESIGNER SECTIONS (below the architect's form; nothing above is changed)
186:## PALETTE (all ids checked with `mcd blocks --check`)
193:| Structure | dark_oak_log | axis=y posts, axis=z beams, axis=x carport beams and mullions |
200:| Utility door | dark_oak_door | facing=west, open=true |
220:## VOCABULARY (helpers; each takes world coordinates; "set" = only into air, per runParts)
225:- `post(x,z,y0=2,y1=4)`: dark_oak_log axis=y.
226:- `glass_bay(x0,x1,z,y0,y1)` or along z: glass_pane fill, only in cells still air.
227:- `slider_gap`: 2 wide x 2 high AIR (y=2..3) with glass_pane at y=4 above. Never closed.
228:- `clerestory(z=8,y=4)`: glass_pane at x=22..24, 26..27, 29..30; dark_oak_log axis=y mullions at x=25 and x=28.
229:- `orange_entry`: orange_concrete at (18,2..4,9) and (20,2..4,9); acacia_door lower half at (19,2,9) and upper half at (19,3,9), facing=north; orange_concrete (19,4,9); smooth_stone (17,1..4,8); white_concrete (21,1..4,8) are the reveals (shell already lays them).
230:- `ledgestone_wall(x0,x1,z=7,y0=1,y1=4)`: mud_bricks, each cell becoming packed_mud with probability 0.25 from a seeded rng; cap mud_brick_slab bottom at y=5 on x=11,12,14,15,17.
233:- `carport()`: posts dark_oak_log (1,1..3,z) for z=8,14,20 (y=1..3), beams dark_oak_log axis=x at y=4 along x=0..9 at z=8,14,20; deck smooth_stone_slab bottom at y=5 x=0..9 z=7..21; fascia dark_oak_slab bottom on x=0, z=7, z=21; floor smooth_stone y=0 x=1..9 z=7..21.
234:- `breeze_screen(z=21)`: for x=1..9, y=1..4, place white_concrete where (x+y) is even, leave the others as air. Corner posts: none.
259:- `galley_kitchen`: counters = smooth_quartz_slab/white_concrete row at y=2 with smoker/furnace/cauldron as appliances; upper cabinets spruce_trapdoor; breakfast bar = spruce_slab top at y=2 on spruce_fence legs; bar stools = birch_slab on iron_trapdoor posts? use dark_oak_fence + birch_slab bottom.
264:## ROOMS (inner air boxes; ceiling y=5 between beams; vault z=14..19 open above)
273:| living (with pit and fireplace) | [11,2,19,21,4,24] (pit x=13..17 z=20..23 is y=1..4 with floor y=0) | terrazzo, pit smooth_quartz | open to dining on z=18/19; atrium doors (19..20,2..3,18); doorway (22,2..4,19..20) east to the corridor; sliders (14..15,2..3,25), (20..21,2..3,25) |
278:| bath 2 (en suite to bed 2) | [29,2,14,30,4,16] | smooth_quartz | door (29,2..3,17) from bedroom 2; clerestory x=31 z=15..16 y=4 |
280:| master bedroom | [23,2,22,30,4,24] | spruce_planks | open to the corridor along z=21/22 at x=23..24; glass x=31 z=21..23; slider (26..27,2..3,25) |
296:## PARTS (12-minute jobs; later parts only add into air; build in this order)
298:1. **parts/shell.mjs, house shell and ground**: dirt at y=-1 over x=0..33 z=0..33 except pool cells (RESERVED); dirt y=0 under the house footprint and atrium; floor y=1 over x=10..31 z=8..25 (terrazzo in public rooms, spruce_planks bedrooms, smooth_quartz baths, none on the pit x=13..17 z=20..23 and the atrium and the chimney; smooth_quartz at y=0 in the pit); perimeter walls: base smooth_stone y=1, body white_concrete y=2..4, header dark_oak_planks y=5 SKIPPING beam-line cells (see header_course); leave every OPENINGS cell as air (entry niche, clerestory cells, windows, sliders, door gaps, ring); door wall z=9 x=17..21 as described; atrium ring walls as dark_oak_planks header + air body for part 4; interior partitions and doorways per ROOMS; ceiling spruce_planks y=5 per ROOMS. Ticks 1, 7, 13 (gaps), 16 (shell).
301:4. **parts/facades.mjs, glazing, posts, entry, feature wall**: `glass_bay` for the south wall, ring, windows; `post` on every beam line of the south wall, 4 corners, ring corners and x=19 at y=4 (lintel); `slider_gap` glazing at y=4; `clerestory`; `orange_entry` with the acacia_door; `ledgestone_wall` and its cap; utility door (dark_oak_door open) at (10,2,10). Ticks 4, 7, 8, 9, 10, 12, 13, 15, 16.
305:## Checklist of parts
306:- [x] 1 shell  - [ ] 2 site  - [ ] 3 roofs  - [ ] 4 facades  - [ ] 5 front  - [ ] 6 back
308:## Notes for workers
312:- The atrium door cells (x=19..20, y=2..3, z=11 and z=18) win over the x=19 post: part 4 puts the post at y=4 only there.
316:- Part 1 (shell, parts/shell.mjs): left AIR for later parts: the four house corner cells (x=10/31, z=8/25, y=2..4, part 4 posts), the whole south wall body y=2..4 (x=10..31, part 4 glazes and posts), the atrium ring body y=2..4 (part 4 glass), the entry-recess cells x=18..20 y=2..4 at z=8 and z=9 (orange_entry), the clerestory y=4 cells x=22..30 at z=8. The y=5 ceiling and header bays on the south wall and the ring are FLOATING in the check until part 3's beam lines and part 4's glass/posts support them.

